## Status, Limits, & Advice
<hr class="section-rule lvl-2">

A short, honest page about where the [CMK compiler]({{_}}/cmk/compiler) stands: how much to trust it, what won't change, and what to do when the frozen defaults don't fit.

### Reporting Bugs
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

The CMK compiler is largely *vibe-coded awk*[^awk], but the test suite is massive, and the specifications, language-semantics, compiler-stages, and the general design is carefully crafted by a real human.  [Please report bugs]({{github.repo_url}}/issues), but not until you've **[confirmed you're using GNU awk!]({{_}}/quickstart/#compatibility-notes)**.

### Stability & Extension
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

Everything that's documented for the compiler is stable and unlikely to change.  Per the rest of the design philosophy, the goal is to [freeze CMK after it's **useful** and **capable of being extended**]({{_}}/but-why#forever-development-considered-harmful) and most future changes are probably optimizations rather than extensions.

If the frozen defaults don't fit your needs, you can [extend a dialect or make it the user-defined default]({{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming/#user-defined-dialects); the [Forks & Versioning]({{_}}/quickstart/#forks-versioning) docs also cover pinning a known-good version.

